// Slideshow stage (features/slideshow/ShowStage.tsx). Rust (src/slideshow_show.rs) computes every
// frame: the layer box of the outgoing / incoming slide, the picture inside it (contain fit,
// Ken Burns, zoom, flip), a circle reveal and overlays; this file only draws the boxes.

export struct SlideVis {
    image: image,
    has-image: bool,
    opacity: float,
    // slide layer (the slide's background box) in stage px
    lx: float,
    ly: float,
    lw: float,
    lh: float,
    // picture box relative to the layer, px
    ix: float,
    iy: float,
    iw: float,
    ih: float,
    // circle reveal radius in px; < 0 = no clip
    clip-r: float,
    // black overlay (slide transition's dimmed exit) and white bloom (blur transition), 0..1
    dim: float,
    glow: float,
}

export struct StageFrame {
    cur: SlideVis,
    prev: SlideVis,
    has-prev: bool,
    bg: color,
    caption-title: string,
    caption-date: string,
    // 0..1, and the rise in px while it fades in
    caption-opacity: float,
    caption-y: float,
}

component SlideLayer inherits Rectangle {
    in property <SlideVis> v;
    in property <color> bg;
    property <bool> circle: root.v.clip-r >= 0;
    property <length> cr: root.v.clip-r * 1px;
    opacity: root.v.opacity;
    // the clip box: the whole layer, or a centred circle of radius clip-r
    clipbox := Rectangle {
        x: root.circle ? root.v.lx * 1px + root.v.lw * 0.5px - root.cr : root.v.lx * 1px;
        y: root.circle ? root.v.ly * 1px + root.v.lh * 0.5px - root.cr : root.v.ly * 1px;
        width: root.circle ? 2 * root.cr : root.v.lw * 1px;
        height: root.circle ? 2 * root.cr : root.v.lh * 1px;
        border-radius: root.circle ? root.cr : 0px;
        clip: true;
        Rectangle {
            x: root.v.lx * 1px - clipbox.x;
            y: root.v.ly * 1px - clipbox.y;
            width: root.v.lw * 1px;
            height: root.v.lh * 1px;
            background: root.bg;
            if root.v.has-image: Image {
                x: root.v.ix * 1px;
                y: root.v.iy * 1px;
                width: root.v.iw * 1px;
                height: root.v.ih * 1px;
                source: root.v.image;
                image-fit: fill;
            }
            if root.v.dim > 0: Rectangle { background: #000000.with-alpha(root.v.dim); }
            if root.v.glow > 0: Rectangle { background: #ffffff.with-alpha(root.v.glow); }
        }
    }
}

export component ShowStage inherits Rectangle {
    in property <StageFrame> frame;
    // stage size in px (Rust lays the slides out for it)
    callback resized(length, length);
    clip: true;
    background: root.frame.bg;
    changed width => { root.resized(self.width, self.height); }
    changed height => { root.resized(self.width, self.height); }
    init => { root.resized(self.width, self.height); }

    if root.frame.has-prev: SlideLayer { v: root.frame.prev; bg: root.frame.bg; }
    SlideLayer { v: root.frame.cur; bg: root.frame.bg; }

    if root.frame.caption-opacity > 0: VerticalLayout {
        x: root.width * 0.05;
        y: root.height * 0.92 - self.preferred-height + root.frame.caption-y * 1px;
        width: root.width * 0.8;
        height: self.preferred-height;
        opacity: root.frame.caption-opacity;
        spacing: 4px;
        Text {
            text: root.frame.caption-title;
            font-family: "Bricolage Grotesque";
            font-weight: 600;
            font-size: Math.clamp(Math.min(root.width, root.height) * 0.032, 16px, 40px);
            color: #ffffff;
            overflow: elide;
        }
        Text {
            text: root.frame.caption-date;
            font-size: Math.clamp(Math.min(root.width, root.height) * 0.017, 11px, 20px);
            color: #ffffffcc;
        }
    }
}
